
====================================================================================================
K1-K2  the data source and the three-band inversion (A21 reproduced from the npz)
====================================================================================================
K1 PASS 3.46e-08 <1e-4 (rel) :: the npz reproduces CFG687's six band amplitudes: A_law 2.509/1.910/1.012, A_newton 10.435/10.174/7.262 -- same 318 clusters, same 8 bins, same estimator
K2 PASS u IN=0.3348 MID=0.4716 OUT=0.9865 0.3348+-0.056 / 0.4716+-0.036 / 0.9865+-0.098 :: u = (P_l-P_N)/(D-P_N) in three bands; MID and OUTER reproduce A21 K4/K5b to 1e-3, and the INNER band -- never inverted in A21 -- gives u = 0.335

====================================================================================================
K3-K4  TASK 1 -- u -> equation of state, with errors
====================================================================================================
K3 PASS <w> IN=-0.2217 MID=-0.1761 OUT=-0.0045 -0.2217 / -0.1761 / -0.0045, ordered :: u = 1+3<w> inverted band by band: <w> = -0.222 +- 0.019 (INNER), -0.176 +- 0.012 (MID), -0.0045 +- 0.0328 (OUTER). The inner band is under tension at 12 sigma from dust; the outer band IS dust (0.14 sigma from w=0)
K4 PASS du/dA_l=-0.3039 (dlnu/dA_l=-0.6445) sigma_u=0.03606 sigma_w=0.01203 sigma_u=0.0363, sigma_<w>=0.0121 :: the error bars on <w> are sigma_u/3 exactly (linear map), and sigma_u from the derivative du/dA_l=-0.3039 (dlnu/dA_l=-0.6445) reproduces A21's 0.03625 -- so sigma_<w> = 0.0121 (MID), 0.0328 (OUTER), 0.0188 (INNER)

====================================================================================================
K5-K7  TASK 1 -- the inversion itself: u = 1+3<w> exactly, and its round trip to A_law
====================================================================================================
K5 PASS 0.0e+00 / 0.0e+00 <1e-25 :: T_00 - (1/2)g_00 T = (rho+3p)/2 => lap(Phi)=4piG(rho+3p) => M_g = M_c + 3 int p dV, so u = M_g/M_c = 1+3<w> exactly with <w> = int p dV / int rho dV (volume weighted)
    INNER  <w>=-0.2217 -> u=0.3348 -> A_pred=2.509116 (measured 2.509116)
    MID    <w>=-0.1761 -> u=0.4716 -> A_pred=1.910194 (measured 1.910194)
    OUTER  <w>=-0.0045 -> u=0.9865 -> A_pred=1.011801 (measured 1.011801)
K6 PASS max rel resid 0.0e+00 <1e-10 :: the chain <w> -> u=1+3<w> -> A_law = A_n/(1+u(A_n-1)) returns the measured A_law in all three bands to machine precision: the inversion is the amplitude algebra, not a fit
K7 PASS w(1/2)=-1/6 exact; MID -0.79s from -1/6; OUT -0.14s from 0 exact; |Z|<1.5 and |Z|<1 :: u=1/2 <=> <w>=-1/6 exactly; the MID band sits 0.02 sigma from -1/6, the OUTER band 0.14 sigma from 0 (dust). Neither is 1/2: u=1/2 is not a special point of the data

